## 5. State Model [CXC-STATE]

### [CXC-STATE-DESIGN] Design Document State

The design document is the source of truth. It is a structured object containing:

```
Design
├── metadata (name, version, target_platform, bus_config)
├── modules[]
│   ├── module_id
│   ├── module_type (e.g., "button_panel", "gauge_panel", "custom")
│   ├── layout (grid position, size, weight within design)
│   ├── config (role, scope, authority — maps to ComposeIO module YAML)
│   └── widgets[]
│       ├── widget_id
│       ├── widget_type (e.g., "ButtonWidget", "GaugeWidget")
│       ├── namespace
│       ├── properties (input_type, led_behavior, state_engine, label, etc.)
│       └── layout (position within module, grid row/col)
├── namespaces[]
│   ├── name
│   ├── state_engine
│   ├── scope
│   ├── authority
│   └── label
├── bindings[]
│   ├── type (simple, compound, event_triggered)
│   └── config (per binding type — see [SPEC:CIO-CONFIG-SCHEMA])
└── connections[]
    └── transport configs for design bus
```

- authority: The design document is modified ONLY through bus commands. No module mutates it directly. The history module captures every mutation for undo/redo.
- persistence: The design document serializes to ComposeIO YAML (see 04-composer-serialization.lts). The in-memory representation and the YAML are isomorphic.

### [CXC-STATE-SELECTION] Selection State

| Namespace | State Engine | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `composer/selection/primary` | `enum: [none, widget, module, binding, namespace]` | What type of object is selected |
| `composer/selection/widget_id` | string | Currently selected widget (empty if none) |
| `composer/selection/module_id` | string | Currently selected module |
| `composer/selection/multi` | list | Multi-selection widget IDs |

- single-select: Default. Clicking a widget selects it and deselects all others.
- multi-select: Shift+click or drag-select. Multiple widgets selected. Property editor shows common properties.
- module-select: Clicking a module header selects the module. Property editor shows module-level config.

### [CXC-STATE-TOOL] Tool Mode State

| Namespace | State Engine | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `composer/tool/mode` | `enum: [select, place, connect, pan]` | Current interaction mode |
| `composer/tool/place_type` | string | Widget type being placed (when mode=place) |

